    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §2808-f, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9519\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to establishing an\nadvanced residential health care for aging adults with medical fragility\ndemonstration program\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Establishes the Advanced Residential Health Care for Aging\nAdults Medical Fragility Demonstration Program for eligible adult resi-\ndential health care facilities with the purpose of improving the quality\nof care for those adults with medical fragility.\n\nSection 2. This act shall take effect immediately.  Adult residential\nhealth care facilities across New York State are faced with difficulties\nrelated to caring for those with medical fragility. Especially for\nfacilities that have a storied history in the state, their facilities\nsometimes lack the modern equipment and technology to advance their care\ncapacity to the next level.\n\nThis bill would primarily support health care facilities that are a\nrecognized nonprofit corporation operating with one hundred and ten\nadult beds or licensed to provide diagnostic and treatment services as\noutlined in the public health law. This serves to enhance the quality of\ncare in these facilities and provides an opportunity for the state to\npositively impact the community and adult health care.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  None\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis legislation will take effect immediately.\n",
